Things could be rigged so that the quest is not optional.  The
obvious way to do that is to require you to have your own quest
artifact in order to enter the new branch, which is what I was
thinking of doing when I wrote the above.  However, I've since
realized that many quest artifacts can theoretically be destroyed
(e.g., by overenchanting), and NetHack has traditionally gone out
of its way to prevent the game from getting into an absolutely
unwinnable state.  Therefore, I propose that the entrance to the
new get-the-bell branch simply check whether you've completed your
quest (the same way your quest leader does when deciding what to
say to you) in order to determine whether you should be allowed
in or not.  If you haven't completed your quest, "You feel unworthy"
when trying to enter the bell branch and a mysterious-force-like
phenomenon sets you back a couple of levels.  Voila, the quest is
not optional.

The hard part is making the new branch interesting enough to
warrant its inclusion.


